    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Magnetism</span> is a fundamental force related to moving electric charges. Natural magnets (lodestone), permanent magnets, and electromagnets are all studied here, along with the force on current-carrying conductors and the basis of electric motors.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Properties of Magnets</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li>Poles: north (N) and south (S). Like poles repel; unlike poles attract.</li><li>Magnetic field lines: from N to S outside the magnet; always continuous closed loops.</li><li>A magnet cannot be split into monopoles — each piece has both N and S poles.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Magnetic Field due to Currents</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li>Straight wire: circular field lines; use Right Hand Grip Rule (thumb along current → fingers show field direction)</li><li>Circular loop: field like a bar magnet at the centre</li><li>Solenoid: uniform field inside like a bar magnet; N pole at end where current is anticlockwise when viewed from that end</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Force on a Current-Carrying Conductor</h3><p class=\"learn-p\"><strong>F = BIL sin θ</strong></p><p class=\"learn-p\">where B = magnetic flux density (T), I = current (A), L = length of conductor in field (m), θ = angle between conductor and field. Maximum force when θ = 90° (conductor ⊥ field).</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Fleming's Rules</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li><strong>Left Hand Rule (motor effect):</strong> Force (thumb), Field (index), Current (middle finger). Used for electric motors.</li><li><strong>Right Hand Rule (generator effect):</strong> Motion (thumb), Field (index), EMF/Current (middle finger). Used for generators.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Magnetic Flux Density</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">B = F/(IL) for conductor ⊥ field. Unit: Tesla (T = N/(A·m)). Magnetic flux Φ = BA cos θ. Unit: Weber (Wb).</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span><strong>Fleming's Rules:</strong> Left Hand = motor (FBI: Force/Thrust, B-field, Current). Right Hand = generator (FBE: Force/Motion, B-field, EMF).</div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span><strong>Summary:</strong> F=BILsinθ. Left Hand Rule (motor). Right Hand Rule (generator). Solenoid: field like bar magnet. Flux Φ=BAcosθ (Weber). B unit: Tesla.</div>",
